    "explanation": "The supplied claim is supported by the visible source. The source states that ponatinib is an approved TKI capable of inhibiting BCR-ABL with the T315I gatekeeper mutation in resistant or relapsed CML, and that in the PACE trial major cytogenetic response occurred in 74% of patients with the T315I mutant. This directly supports a predictive sensitivity/response relationship for ponatinib in CML with BCR::ABL1 and ABL1 T315I. The source does not explicitly use the word “somatic,” but the context of resistant/relapsed CML and baseline BCR-ABL mutations is consistent with an acquired/somatic disease context; no visible evidence contradicts the somatic framing. No unresolved role-report items were provided, and no unsupported efficacy claims were inferred beyond the cited response rate.",
